[{:db/id "q-345179/selection/e3032423a23a8b851a35b8990c336e75c22a605c026d0dd243ce7e45643943ad" :answer/id #uuid "2ab010f3-456a-5e0c-9b0c-219fb0dd018f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda =0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345179/selection/7bc7f76cab7247cffab6df5d70eb7ffea5df32aca230b77ed32e88734e31abbf" :answer/id #uuid "0e2ae26a-1b8b-5c90-b903-56a731e5253a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda =0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345179/selection/6c6fa70db3877ba1a09ded06280bd30bb957e1a4fe89b81e0cc6e34570460864" :answer/id #uuid "542228d8-9394-5628-85bc-7c92489f493e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda =0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345179/selection/2395ef9f72e3d08b0c4cdd360d7fa0165475a662b4790e89446a7446ea9c17d6" :answer/id #uuid "f6eac7a7-c4db-53e3-a6d6-07fed3b758d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345179/selection/4df1eada7885007afbd1f61c2aa4829a54c8f0924b6bee13f52f6bba5483e3a3" :answer/id #uuid "65ab8e46-d600-5e51-8132-e306c0c36258" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda =0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345179/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "bbf9966b-f322-567d-8f0c-4c084e537336" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-345179/selection/e3032423a23a8b851a35b8990c336e75c22a605c026d0dd243ce7e45643943ad" :answer-field/choices ["q-345179/selection/e3032423a23a8b851a35b8990c336e75c22a605c026d0dd243ce7e45643943ad" "q-345179/selection/7bc7f76cab7247cffab6df5d70eb7ffea5df32aca230b77ed32e88734e31abbf" "q-345179/selection/6c6fa70db3877ba1a09ded06280bd30bb957e1a4fe89b81e0cc6e34570460864" "q-345179/selection/2395ef9f72e3d08b0c4cdd360d7fa0165475a662b4790e89446a7446ea9c17d6" "q-345179/selection/4df1eada7885007afbd1f61c2aa4829a54c8f0924b6bee13f52f6bba5483e3a3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345179" :question/id #uuid "4349166c-f0d5-5e7f-a33b-9d1b5253d94c" :question/math-academy-id "q-345179" :question/problem "$$\n8x{y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nFind the indicial equation for a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above." :question/worked-solution "If $x=0$ is a regular singular point of a second-order homogeneous linear differential equation, then the method of Frobenius states that there is at least one solution of the form\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda $ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants.\n\nSubstituting this solution and its derivatives into the ODE, collecting like terms, and setting coefficients equal to zero, we obtain: \n\n- the indicial equation from the coefficients of the $n=0$ term for arbitrary ${a}_{0},$ and\n\n- a recurrence formula from the coefficients of the $n\\ge 1$ terms.\n\n**Step 1**: Write the solution $y$ as a Frobenius power series:\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the derivatives ${y}^{′}$ and ${y}^{″}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n})}^{′}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\ {y}^{″} & ={({\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1})}^{′}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Rewrite all the series in the equation so that they use the same index of summation, the powers of $x$ are the same, and the indices start at the same value.\n\nThe terms of the differential equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x{y}^{″} & =8x\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }8((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ -2{y}^{′} & =-2\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ y & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the $y$ term, we change the index of the summation by writing $n=m-1.$ This gives\n\n$$\ny={\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{\\lambda +m-1}.\n$$\n\nThen, replacing $m$ with $n$ (since it does not matter which letter we use) gives\n\n$$\ny={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\n$$\n\nNow, isolating the $n=0$ terms for the other terms in the ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x{y}^{″} & =8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ -2{y}^{′} & =-2\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}-2\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda -2\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form ${x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$ for some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ 2(4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda ){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficients of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda ){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 4{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345179/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94dc48ed-1523-5b21-aedb-d920ecd4b8a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345179"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274/selection/85b263045c41da9965dc2f07bcbeff46ad9a172f8491b8fd0ff20b714478890a" :answer/id #uuid "7371b5bd-28ca-5a56-9acc-5291ed8a077b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9{\\lambda }^{2}-7\\lambda +5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274/selection/5b63991868be3870edbf846002065a0fcffc09a493cc7d312d4e80d4996873a6" :answer/id #uuid "87bc108f-b5d1-57f9-8739-6368340a6b4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda -5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274/selection/c7fcc933d135cf24ffff5226049a8e0dce81d9c2a352fd56d1f87f858a449900" :answer/id #uuid "f00d1a52-5aea-5a6e-ae70-6cbc7354436b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{\\lambda }^{2}+9\\lambda +5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274/selection/a92a084c216af2f237d520a2b3c49f7103c1d29c015de4a323fed9bfb693a612" :answer/id #uuid "515ad26f-a81c-5fb0-a35b-e817918a84aa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +7=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274/selection/434d8f9748fc2b95a6d5a220ae94463208f2d92188ca3cb59cbe0143a2bd0257" :answer/id #uuid "7288ba6a-57a8-58cd-ae31-daf95092e896" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7{\\lambda }^{2}-9\\lambda +5=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8bf6155f-e11f-5ac9-a1d9-64e132c7a1fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-345274/selection/434d8f9748fc2b95a6d5a220ae94463208f2d92188ca3cb59cbe0143a2bd0257" :answer-field/choices ["q-345274/selection/85b263045c41da9965dc2f07bcbeff46ad9a172f8491b8fd0ff20b714478890a" "q-345274/selection/5b63991868be3870edbf846002065a0fcffc09a493cc7d312d4e80d4996873a6" "q-345274/selection/c7fcc933d135cf24ffff5226049a8e0dce81d9c2a352fd56d1f87f858a449900" "q-345274/selection/a92a084c216af2f237d520a2b3c49f7103c1d29c015de4a323fed9bfb693a612" "q-345274/selection/434d8f9748fc2b95a6d5a220ae94463208f2d92188ca3cb59cbe0143a2bd0257"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345274" :question/id #uuid "e617971d-af12-59ac-a1e1-3a955cbb7317" :question/math-academy-id "q-345274" :question/problem "$$\n-7{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+(x-5)y=0\n$$\n\nFind the indicial equation for a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above." :question/worked-solution "If $x=0$ is a regular singular point of a second-order homogeneous linear differential equation, then the method of Frobenius states that there is at least one solution of the form\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda $ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants.\n\nSubstituting this solution and its derivatives into the ODE, collecting like terms, and setting coefficients equal to zero, we obtain: \n\n- the indicial equation from the coefficients of the $n=0$ term for arbitrary ${a}_{0},$ and\n\n- a recurrence formula from the coefficients of the $n\\ge 1$ terms.\n\n**Step 1**: Write the solution $y$ as a Frobenius power series:\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the derivatives ${y}^{′}$ and ${y}^{″}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ {y}^{″} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Rewrite all the series so that they use the same index of summation.\n\nThe terms of the differential equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =-7{x}^{2}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }7((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ 2x{y}^{′} & =2x\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ (x-5)y & =(x-5){\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n+1}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }5{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the first sum of the $y$ term, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n(x-5)y={\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{\\lambda +m}-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }5{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\n$$\n\nThen, replacing $m$ with $n$ (since it does not matter which letter we use) and isolating the $n=0$ term gives\n\n$$\n(x-5)y={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n}-5{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, isolating the $n=0$ terms for the other terms in the ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =-7({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }7((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ 2x{y}^{′} & =2\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-7({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+2\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-5{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (-7{\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +2\\lambda -5){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (-7{\\lambda }^{2}+9\\lambda -5){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form\n${x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$\nfor some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -5){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ (-7{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -5){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficient of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-7{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda -5){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 7{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +5 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345274/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94dc48ed-1523-5b21-aedb-d920ecd4b8a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345274"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275/selection/0f479c88b0059668a3efddc6504351a58ea6eb35fbf727add3ddaf522ba63885" :answer/id #uuid "6fed37d1-695f-531c-ba37-e5fe6469c63f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +2=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275/selection/2a614c8ba7633e835869126d39b91b1dbd1d2af5bbc7cfab56ea7d60075f3bab" :answer/id #uuid "8b890205-8321-5f75-91cf-1d2b2f8fa50c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda -4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275/selection/a1ee20e5647bc45c6b9c69ce082fb9417b5d26156f7f886522c132eee4ea1ab9" :answer/id #uuid "ff0d025c-885e-5c77-a0c3-66ce7e898705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275/selection/45c01b563b690af04865b355384903bb3b5a787e57de5c5b485a28a454813f7e" :answer/id #uuid "60434cbf-971a-5f51-9afa-2d76acb8bc2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275/selection/a010ff99b8b3041d2dcc04c0f89f6ef0666fa09bd0137d330c736345e1a90c74" :answer/id #uuid "94a33107-424f-5e31-bc62-ad7d7608426d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda +4=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ed783431-ea58-54a8-acb5-7ce3cbfaec77" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-345275/selection/45c01b563b690af04865b355384903bb3b5a787e57de5c5b485a28a454813f7e" :answer-field/choices ["q-345275/selection/0f479c88b0059668a3efddc6504351a58ea6eb35fbf727add3ddaf522ba63885" "q-345275/selection/2a614c8ba7633e835869126d39b91b1dbd1d2af5bbc7cfab56ea7d60075f3bab" "q-345275/selection/a1ee20e5647bc45c6b9c69ce082fb9417b5d26156f7f886522c132eee4ea1ab9" "q-345275/selection/45c01b563b690af04865b355384903bb3b5a787e57de5c5b485a28a454813f7e" "q-345275/selection/a010ff99b8b3041d2dcc04c0f89f6ef0666fa09bd0137d330c736345e1a90c74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345275" :question/id #uuid "90cbc2a3-a8f6-533e-a406-eaa596a5ef91" :question/math-academy-id "q-345275" :question/problem "$$\n2{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-11x{y}^{′}-(x-4)y=0\n$$\n\nFind the indicial equation for a Frobenius series solution about the regular singular point $x=0$ of the differential equation above." :question/worked-solution "If $x=0$ is a regular singular point of a second-order homogeneous linear differential equation, then the method of Frobenius states that there is at least one solution of the form\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda $ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants.\n\nSubstituting this solution and its derivatives into the ODE, collecting like terms, and setting coefficients equal to zero, we obtain: \n\n- the indicial equation from the coefficients of the $n=0$ term for arbitrary ${a}_{0},$ and\n\n- a recurrence formula from the coefficients of the $n\\ge 1$ terms.\n\n**Step 1**: Write the solution $y$ as a Frobenius power series:\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**: Compute the derivatives ${y}^{′}$ and ${y}^{″}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ {y}^{″} & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 3**: Rewrite all the series so that they use the same index of summation.\n\nThe terms of the differential equation are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =2{x}^{2}\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n-1)(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-2} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }2((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -11x{y}^{′} & =-11x\\cdot {\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }11(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -(x-4)y & =-(x-4){\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\  & =-{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n+1}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }4{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the first sum of the $y$ term, we change the index of the summation by writing $m=n+1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n-(x-4)y=-{\\sum }_{m=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{m-1}{x}^{\\lambda +m}+{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }4{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\n$$\n\nThen, replacing $m$ with $n$ (since it does not matter which letter we use) and isolating the $n=0$ term gives\n\n$$\n-(x-4)y=-{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n-1}{x}^{\\lambda +n}+4{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }4{a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, isolating the $n=0$ terms for the other terms in the ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =2({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }2((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ -11x{y}^{′} & =-11\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }-11(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }-11\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+4{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (2{\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda -11\\lambda +4){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +4){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }. & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form\n${x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$\nfor some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +4){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ (2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +4){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 5**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficient of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +4){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345275/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94dc48ed-1523-5b21-aedb-d920ecd4b8a6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345275"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282/selection/780e1ca34c143672fdea94b4ec5ce0b161ed8cf7a561144b6f2e209127e40ed0" :answer/id #uuid "3a4dc535-0eb1-5dee-9bbe-a83e7265196d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+2/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282/selection/24c5a7d9cd2421471ad6cf3243bf6efe702880f1c17be337338bf697414d9785" :answer/id #uuid "b9d72f0e-6736-5785-b165-f1d941fa7945" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282/selection/f7002dc6121b6cd7464780710382da5d91bd21180e8121c46b21bb02ba618ac3" :answer/id #uuid "3d293a48-75e5-59ab-84d4-21d5c488e9b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-2/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282/selection/4261e56c75bebbabf8058d2d57d40b7e853e7efc70bfe4ac4d9e443ec6b0b638" :answer/id #uuid "e5ebbca4-a526-5c9c-b10a-86f67bb9ac66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1/3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282/selection/0f903ec07c20fd2a3198b9f6c43a0256c78e7434291b7925ad860f5be0f03bcf" :answer/id #uuid "1f5ccd10-4eff-5cb6-a9a6-de50b2c40e20" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-1/2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "231855a0-5bb1-5fe1-b7dc-a7c87693d1f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-345282/selection/24c5a7d9cd2421471ad6cf3243bf6efe702880f1c17be337338bf697414d9785" :answer-field/choices ["q-345282/selection/780e1ca34c143672fdea94b4ec5ce0b161ed8cf7a561144b6f2e209127e40ed0" "q-345282/selection/24c5a7d9cd2421471ad6cf3243bf6efe702880f1c17be337338bf697414d9785" "q-345282/selection/f7002dc6121b6cd7464780710382da5d91bd21180e8121c46b21bb02ba618ac3" "q-345282/selection/4261e56c75bebbabf8058d2d57d40b7e853e7efc70bfe4ac4d9e443ec6b0b638" "q-345282/selection/0f903ec07c20fd2a3198b9f6c43a0256c78e7434291b7925ad860f5be0f03bcf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345282" :question/id #uuid "8e0a963c-cee9-51b7-abf2-4e51362ad265" :question/math-academy-id "q-345282" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n6{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}+(6x+1)y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a Frobenius series solution to the differential equation, where ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants determined by substitution?\n\n*Hint: Substituting a trial Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ x{y}^{′} & =\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ (6x+1)y & ={a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(6{a}_{n-1}+{a}_{n}){x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $x=0$ is a regular singular point of a second-order homogeneous linear differential equation, then the method of Frobenius states that there is at least one solution of the form\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda $ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants.\n\nSubstituting this solution and its derivatives into the ODE, collecting like terms, and setting coefficients equal to zero, we obtain:\n\n- the indicial equation from the coefficients of the $n=0$ term for arbitrary ${a}_{0},$ and\n\n- a recurrence formula from the coefficients of the $n\\ge 1$ terms.\n\nWe are given the three terms of the ODE as power series with the $n=0$ term isolated in each.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}^{2}{y}^{″} & =6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }6((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n}, \\\\ x{y}^{′} & =\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n} \\\\ (6x+1)y & ={a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(6{a}_{n-1}+{a}_{n}){x}^{\\lambda +n}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we continue from this point.\n\n**Step 1**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (6{\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +\\lambda +1){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & = \\\\ (6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda } & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form\n${x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$\nfor some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda }+{x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ (6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficient of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can determine a solution. Solving the indicial equation for the roots, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +1 & =0 \\\\ (3\\lambda -1)(2\\lambda -1) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the two Frobenius series solutions are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/2}\\,\\text{and}\\,y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the constants ${a}_{n}$ are to be determined separately in each of the two cases.\n\nOf the given options, the correct answer is\n$y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+1/3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-345282/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a5d6ee-cc3b-5473-8cfc-0ccecd631449"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405/selection/c793d5c824c3d3c4c5028f0f5b309c2d601c175870d1b38c92bfe1dc5c6fcdad" :answer/id #uuid "970f834c-6c09-5393-a88f-090dc0f357c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+3/8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405/selection/ce3a1782576919c817c2281b219b45cc2d9f960dacebb2b7e5a20b7cdf61f3ee" :answer/id #uuid "e1a00e87-12a2-5f1d-8500-3d36da8b73db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-3/8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405/selection/4a0902bce002e70c766eaf1c48ee6d3f287c1e3f4b85936b7ca306286aaf107a" :answer/id #uuid "137347a1-4cbb-56f1-be31-8639211d54c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n-3/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405/selection/bb3267a86845864baf956adb09573e6bc560cdc77b9246f11c6b586beb2f38e6" :answer/id #uuid "ff3faa25-b8ad-5a88-90a1-c9e7e9d35b2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+3/4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405/selection/2f2e32a4762ff3091d8dcc63b2a1f632787c03c2b20a336bb30c5ec4336d49c5" :answer/id #uuid "1d129f7b-f743-5ea7-acdb-8c96e9f722b1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+5/8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "382e14c1-f61f-5129-bbd0-5d40fb1b2336" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-345405/selection/c793d5c824c3d3c4c5028f0f5b309c2d601c175870d1b38c92bfe1dc5c6fcdad" :answer-field/choices ["q-345405/selection/c793d5c824c3d3c4c5028f0f5b309c2d601c175870d1b38c92bfe1dc5c6fcdad" "q-345405/selection/ce3a1782576919c817c2281b219b45cc2d9f960dacebb2b7e5a20b7cdf61f3ee" "q-345405/selection/4a0902bce002e70c766eaf1c48ee6d3f287c1e3f4b85936b7ca306286aaf107a" "q-345405/selection/bb3267a86845864baf956adb09573e6bc560cdc77b9246f11c6b586beb2f38e6" "q-345405/selection/2f2e32a4762ff3091d8dcc63b2a1f632787c03c2b20a336bb30c5ec4336d49c5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-345405" :question/id #uuid "9508d6b9-6f8e-5a5e-a6f0-0250ebe3d581" :question/math-academy-id "q-345405" :question/problem "Consider the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n8x{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}-2y=0\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is a Frobenius series solution to the differential equation, where ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants determined by substitution?\n\n*Hint: Substituting a trial Frobenius series solution into each term of the ODE, we obtain*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x{y}^{″} & =8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ 5{y}^{′} & =5\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ -2y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-2{a}_{n-1}){x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If $x=0$ is a regular singular point of a second-order homogeneous linear differential equation, then the method of Frobenius states that there is at least one solution of the form\n\n$$\ny={x}^{\\lambda }{\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda $ and ${a}_{n}$ for $n=0,1,2,…$ are constants.\n\nSubstituting this solution and its derivatives into the ODE, collecting like terms, and setting coefficients equal to zero, we obtain:\n\n- the indicial equation from the coefficients of the $n=0$ term for arbitrary ${a}_{0},$ and\n\n- a recurrence formula from the coefficients of the $n\\ge 1$ terms.\n\nWe are given the three terms of the ODE as power series with the $n=0$ term isolated in each.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8x{y}^{″} & =8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }8((\\lambda +n)^{2}-(\\lambda +n)){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ 5{y}^{′} & =5\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }5(\\lambda +n){a}_{n}{x}^{\\lambda +n-1}, \\\\ -2y & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }(-2{a}_{n-1}){x}^{\\lambda +n-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we continue from this point.\n\n**Step 1**: Consolidate all the series into a single series that is equal to $0.$\n\nCollecting the terms for $n=0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+5\\lambda {a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-8\\lambda +5\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & = \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1} & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, collecting terms for $n\\ge 1,$ we obtain an infinite series of the form\n${x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n},$\nfor some ${b}_{n}(\\lambda ),$ $n\\ge 1.$\nTherefore, substituting into the homogeneous ODE, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda ){a}_{0}{x}^{\\lambda -1}+{x}^{\\lambda -1}{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0 \\\\ (8{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda ){a}_{0}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}(\\lambda ){x}^{n} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 2**:  Set the coefficients of the series equal to $0.$\n\nSetting the coefficient of the $n=0$ term equal to $0$ with arbitrary ${a}_{0}\\ne 0,$ we obtain the indicial equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(8{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda ){a}_{0} & =0 \\\\ 8{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can determine a solution. Solving the indicial equation for the roots, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8{\\lambda }^{2}-3\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (8\\lambda -3) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda  & =0,\\frac{3}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the two Frobenius series solutions are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n}\\,\\text{and}\\,y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+3/8},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere the constants ${a}_{n}$ are to be determined separately in each of the two cases.\n\nOf the given options, the correct answer is\n$y(x)={\\sum }_{n=0}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}{x}^{n+3/8}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-345405/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "12a5d6ee-cc3b-5473-8cfc-0ccecd631449"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-345405"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
